description:
Generic org-unit aggregation workflow. Loads a published GeoZarr dataset over a time range, spatially aggregates its variable within each GeoJSON feature (e.g. a DHIS2 organisation unit) using the chosen method, and exports the result as a DHIS2 `dataValueSet` JSON payload.

Each feature's GeoJSON `id` becomes the DHIS2 `orgUnit`, each time step becomes a DHIS2 `period` (formatted according to `period_type`), and the dataset variable becomes the `value`. Aggregation is performed at the dataset's native temporal resolution, so set `period_type` to match it (e.g. `month` for a monthly dataset, `day` for a daily one).

Usage — call this process as the result of a process graph, passing your dataset id and org-unit GeoJSON:

{
  "agg": {
    "process_id": "aggregate_to_dhis2_json",
    "arguments": {
      "dataset_id": "era5land_precipitation_monthly",
      "temporal_extent": ["2025-01-01", "2025-12-31"],
      "geometries": { "type": "FeatureCollection", "features": [ ... ] },
      "data_element_id": "fbfJHSPpUQD",
      "method": "mean",
      "period_type": "month"
    },
    "result": true
  }
}
